  "notes": "Cash basis (modified cash). Governmental funds Total Major Governmental Funds column of Exhibit D (p4). All funds including School Nutrition are governmental special revenue funds; no business-type fund, so business_type is null. Printed Total Receipts on Exhibit D read as 5,666,302 (fund columns sum to 5,666,302, and 5,666,302 - 5,557,079 = 109,223 change in net position). Local Sources split into categories using the fund schedules (Exhibits F-L, now including the Activity Fund schedule Exhibit I on p9); each split sums to the printed line. Activity Fund local receipts 93,256 split: interest 581, admissions 8,048 (student activity receipts), contributions 84,627; spending 178,023 on one line (student activity spending). Interfund loans (General +110,000, Special Building -110,000 and +60,566, Bond -60,566) net to zero in the total column and are not in top-level fields; recorded in detail as other financing. Transfers 200,000 = General Fund to School Nutrition 95,000, Activity 55,000, Depreciation 50,000 (verified against Exhibits F, H, I, J). General Fund Exhibit F total disbursements 4,724,879 exclude the 200,000 transfers (no hidden transfers in spending). Exhibit F total receipts 5,085,351 includes the 110,000 interfund loan. Employee Benefit fund spending 2,603 is shown under Instruction in Exhibit D. Investments 50,000 are in the roll-forward balance (cash and investments combined), not added separately. Roll-forward: 2,704,369 + 5,666,302 - 5,557,079 + 200,000 - 200,000 = 2,813,592. Balance sheet from Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis (Exhibit A, no liabilities). Read pages 1-12 of 12"
